Provided a planning problem, consisting of an initial state of the world, a final goal and a set of constraints, your task is to provide a valid sequence of actions that solves the planning problem, i.e., bringing about the goal of the problem while satisfying all constraints.To solve the problem, think step-by-step.The format of each action in the plan should be: 'ActionName Argument1 ... ArgumentN', where each argument is an element of the domain. Write each action of a plan in a separate line. Delineate the plan with one top line and one bottom line containing only 3  '`' characters.You need to provide an optimal plan, i.e., a valid plan whose length is equal or less than the length of any other valid plan.

You are an agent navigating locations inside a house. Each location is a room that may contain several objects and object receptacles. It is possible to pickup some objects and place them into appropriate receptacles. Moreover, it may be possible for you to heat, cool, toggle and slice some of the objects or look at them under a light. Your task is to bring about some object-receptacle configuration, or heat, cool or look at some object under a light.

The available actions are the following:
	"look a l": Agent a checks location l.
	"inventory a": Agent a checks its inventory.
	"examinereceptacle a r": Agent a checks receptacle r.
	"examineobject a o": Agent a checks object o.
	"gotolocation a ls le": Agent a moves from location ls to location le.
	"openobject a l r": Agent a opens receptacle r at location l.
	"closeobject a l r": Agent a closes receptacle r at location l.
	"pickupobject a l o r": Agent a picks up object o which is in receptacle r at location l.
	"putobject a l o r ot rt": Agent a puts object o (whose type is ot) in receptacle r (whose type is rt) at location l.
	"cleanobject a l r o": Agent a cleans object o in receptacle r at location l.
	"heatobject a l r o": Agent a heats object o in receptacle r at location l.
	"coolobject a l r o": Agent a cools object o in receptacle r at location l.
	"toggleobject a l o r": Agent a toggles object o in receptacle r at location l.
	"sliceobject a l co ko": Agent a slices object co using object ko at location l.
	"help a": Agent a checks itself.

An action may only be performed if its preconditions are met.
The actions of this domain have the following preconditions:
	"look": you may only perform this action with you (agent a) are in location l.
	"inventory": you may perform this anytime.
	"examinereceptacle": you may only perform this action if there is a location l such that you (agent a) are in l and receptacle r is in l.
	"examineobject": you may perform this action if there is a location l and a receptacle r such that you (agent a) are in l, r is in l, object o is in r, and r is opened or is not openable. The only other possibility to perform this action is to be holding object o.
	"gotolocation": you may only perform this action if you (agent a) are in location ls.
	"openobject": you may only perform this action if you (agent a) are in location l, receptacle r is in l, r is openable and r is not opened.
	"closeobject": you may only perform this action if you (agent a) are in location l, receptacle r is in l, r is openable and r is opened.
	"pickupobject": you may only perform this action if you (agent a) are in location l, receptacle r is in l, object o is in r, you are not holding anything, o is pickupable, and r is opened or not openable.
	"putobject": you may only perform this action if you (agent a) are in location l, receptacle r is in l, you are holding object o, r is opened or not openable, o is of type ot, r is of type rt and receptacles of type rt may contain objects of type ot.
	"cleanobject": you may only perform this action if you (agent a) are in location l, receptacle r is in l, you are holding object o, o is cleanable, and r is a sink basin according to its type.
	"heatobject": you may only perform this action if you (agent a) are in location l, receptacle r is in l, you are holding object o, o is heatable, and r is a microwave according to its type.
	"coolobject": you may only perform this action if you (agent a) are in location l, receptacle r is in l, you are holding object o, o is coolable, and r is a fridge according to its type.
	"toggleobject": you may only perform this action if you (agent a) are in location l, receptacle r is in l, you are holding object o and o is togglable.
	"sliceobject": you may only perform this action if you (agent a) are in location l, object co is in l, you are holding object ko, co is sliceable, and ko is a knife or a butterknife according to its type.
	"help": you may perform this anytime.

The effects of an action are brought about after the action is performed.
An effect may be conditional, in the sense that it manifests only if some conditions hold.
 The actions of this domain have the following effects:
	"look": after performing this action location l is checked.
	"inventory": after performing this action agent a is checked.
	"examinereceptacle": after performing this action receptacle r is checked.
	"examineobject": after performing this action object o is checked.
	"gotolocation": after performing this action (i) agent a is no longer at location ls and (ii) agent a is at location le.
	"openobject": after performing this action (i) receptacle r is opened and (ii) receptacle r is checked.
	"closeobject": after performing this action receptacle r is no longer opened.
	"pickupobject": after performing this action (i) object o is no longer in receptacle r, (ii) you are holding object o, and (iii) object o is not longer in location l.
	"putobject": after performing this action (i) object o is in receptacle r, (ii) object o is in location l, and (iii) you are not holding any object.
	"cleanobject": after performing this action object o is clean.
	"heatobject": after performing this action object o is hot.
	"coolobject": after performing this action object o is cool.
	"toggleobject": after performing this action (i) object o is turned on, if it was previously off, (ii) object o is turned off, if it was previously on, and (iii) object o is considered "toggled".
	"sliceobject": after performing this action object o is sliced.
	"helpobject": after performing this action agent a is checked.

